{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLFxvoZcHAAU7cjCLiCs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the crash: `sympy.zeros(4,2).is_upper` now returns `True` instead of raising `IndexError`.\n\nThe change is one line in `sympy/matrices/matrices.py:1115`. The column loop now stops at the matrix width, using `range(min(i, self.cols))` instead of `range(i)`. Before, tall matrices made it look up column indices that don't exist, like the (3,2) entry in the issue.\n\nI checked the result on two cases:\n- `zeros(4,2).is_upper` → `True`\n- a 4x2 matrix with a nonzero entry below the diagonal → `False`\n\nI ran only the existing matrix tests whose names mention \"upper\", \"lower\" or \"triangular\" (4 tests), and they pass. I didn't run the full matrix test file, and I didn't add a test for this case because test files were off-limits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":895,"cache_read_input_tokens":18801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":895},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3043cebc-9a38-4faf-aeb8-784a42f5de70","uuid":"8a681445-11ec-42b6-b1de-0da54f6ae26e","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:32:00.642Z","request_id":"req_011ChLFxvfdtQVSze6DEVsWm"}
